WEBVTT

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:11.720
Whoo!

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.680
In the heart of Africa, a young family is heading for an epic adventure.

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:27.160
They are moving with their three children to a remote Kenyan wilderness.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:32.240
Mum, Saba, is here to run a safari camp...

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:32.360
Welcome!

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:36.600
..While Dad, Frank, is helping to protect elephants.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.960
Collar's almost on.

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.480
Now the scary bit.

00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:45.080
But raising a family and running a business in the bush is going to be a massive challenge.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.840
There are monkeys in the kitchen...

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:49.200
Oh, you monkeys, I'm going to kill you!

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.680
Floods threatening the camp...

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.240
It's looking like it's going to be a mega storm.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.480
Medical emergencies...

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.200
It's bad and it needs urgent action.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.360
And wildlife in need of help...

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:02.720
And my heart really is in my mouth.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.480
It's going to be a huge gamble.

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:11.720
Will the business survive Saba's first season in charge?

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:12.360
Oh, my God.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.480
Hello!

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.040
This time, high season is in full swing.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:18.640
Everything has to be, you know, super, super, super.

00:01:17.840 --> 00:01:24.000
But drought has forced the main attraction to leave the reserve.

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:29.480
It becomes a bit of a challenge for us, because, you know, there aren't that many elephants.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:35.240
It spells disaster for the business, and for the elephants.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:41.760
Poachers were spotted this morning and they ran from their camp.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.000
The team's battle with poachers becomes critical.

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.080
They're out there, they're right on the front line.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:05.640
There's a drought in Samburu... ..and elephants are leaving the reserve.

00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:12.400
It's bad news for Elephant Watch Camp.

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:15.920
It's really shocking how dry it is.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:20.840
Every day we see more and more of the mudflats and there's just no sign of any more rain.

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:24.400
It's just so dry and sparse and barren out there.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:34.040
Of course, it's impacting hard on the elephants and it will get worse as the year goes on, they'll be much more spread out and they'll be moving much further away out of the reserve.

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:43.440
Saba's business is all about elephant watching and this is their busiest time of year.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:48.960
But without the stars of the show, Saba is worried.

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:57.240
Camp guide, Alfred, is setting off to collect the latest arrivals.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.680
Today, we're heading out to this airstrip, which is the Oryx airstrip.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:05.960
I'm picking a couple that is coming in today for three days.

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.840
There are three different airstrips near the reserve.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:17.160
Today's guests are due to land at the one closest to camp and Alfred's keen to get there in good time.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:27.320
We have to be there, like, half an hour before because they're quite erratic, they have other stopovers and sometimes they don't keep their times properly.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:32.040
Bush airstrips are a basic affair.

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:35.120
The runway is cleared out of the scrub.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:43.440
There is no arrivals lounge, no refreshments and no shade.

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.440
So, it's important to arrive before your guests.

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:50.840
While Alfred's waiting for the plane, Saba receives a call in camp.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:51.240
Hello?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.920
'Hi...'

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.000
Hi, how are you?

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:03.360
We were told they were going to land at Oryx.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:05.560
It's not good news.

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:06.200
All right.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.240
All right, thank you.

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.000
Bye.

00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:16.160
The airline who was bringing our people this morning has landed at a different airstrip.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:20.200
(It's terrible. )

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:23.200
This is a pain.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.840
Go like the wind, but not too fast.

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:32.280
That's, it's a disaster, disaster, disaster.

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.320
Because everything's now upside down.

00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:39.800
The airstrip the plane has landed at is an hour away.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.560
And the temperature is soaring into the 40s.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:51.360
We have to now fly like a bat from hell.

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:59.720
The clients might be very unhappy if they are dropped somewhere and nobody picks them up, so... it's, it's quite... something.

00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:03.800
This is just one of those things that should not happen.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:26.040
In Kenya's Samburu National Reserve, it hasn't rained for over three months.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.880
The plains are turning into dustbowls.

00:05:29.920 --> 00:05:37.600
It's a tough time for the elephants.

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:45.000
Many of them are leaving the reserve to look for food.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:49.640
And they're heading into danger.

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:58.160
Saba's husband, Frank, works for conservation charity, Save The Elephants.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:02.160
He's worried about their safety.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:17.640
What we've got here in Samburu is this really critical population, it's one of the best studied populations in, in Africa, and... ..we need to defend this population.

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:33.360
This area has been really badly hit in the past by this surge of poaching that's gone across Africa, and... what I'd really love to see is that this year, we have no more elephants killed in Samburu.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:45.320
But if the elephants leave the protected areas, they risk being killed for their ivory.

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:52.760
Only six weeks ago, a 25-year-old bull was lost.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.200
He was shot so close to the reserve, the poachers fled before they took his tusks.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:06.680
Frank wants to catch them before they strike again.

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:10.800
He's joined Saba's father, Iain.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:14.360
They're heading to the scene of the crime in search of evidence.

00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:27.560
Iain Douglas-Hamilton was the head of anti-poaching in Uganda at the height of the ivory crisis in the '80s.

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:31.520
He pioneered the use of forensics to bring poachers to justice.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.880
This is it, I think.

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:35.120
Ja, look at this.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:35.680
Yeah, this is definitely Koitalel.

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:45.520
After six weeks of baking temperatures and hungry scavengers, the carcass has been reduced to a pile of dry bones.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:50.240
If they can find bullets in these remains they have a chance of putting those responsible behind bars.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:57.000
Well, we're searching now for, er, metal, particularly for the bullets.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.080
I test to see if it's working against my knee...

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:01.920
..because I've got a metal plate in here.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:13.520
What we want to find is a bullet and we want to tell what calibre that bullet was and therefore what weapon it was fired from.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:18.360
The bullet could have dropped out anywhere here by now.

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:19.320
Did you find a bullet hole over there?

00:08:18.440 --> 00:08:23.120
We've got three bullet holes in his shoulder here.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.560
As you remember, his, er...

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.160
The bullet went right through there.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.520
..His right shoulder.

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:29.440
If you remember, had lots of...

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.600
It came through from that side and this was the exit hole, here.

00:08:32.919 --> 00:08:35.880
Yeah.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:42.640
Well, it's quite stunning to see how, how much it's already been, it's already been pulled apart and everything disintegrated.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.400
It's like archaeology.

00:08:48.680 --> 00:08:56.000
BEEPING It looks like nice dry earth that would be really easy to dig into...

00:08:55.560 --> 00:09:04.840
This is a, this is a corpse, really, that's, that's sunk into the ground here and made it really, really hard.

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:10.720
BEEPING It's like digging into sandstone.

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.240
That's it.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.360
Here's the bullet.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.320
Wow.

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:18.720
One of them, anyway.

00:09:17.960 --> 00:09:22.360
That's a bit distorted, unfortunately.

00:09:21.520 --> 00:09:22.800
This bullet is useless.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:27.680
To make a conviction, they need to find undamaged ones.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.680
They must keep on searching.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:33.400
At the airstrip, Alfred has met his guests.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:39.440
Sorry, we were on the wrong airstrip.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:47.080
You have to really drink a lot, because you don't realise how much you get dehydrated out here.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:50.480
It is quite hot.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:56.280
The camp relies on guest recommendations for future business.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:10:03.480
Unhappy guests means bookings may suffer.

00:10:02.640 --> 00:10:07.480
Every detail must be perfect.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:12.240
Oh, what a beautiful new mat.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:13.320
That really does look good, doesn't it?

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:17.440
'Just on the lake, I think five minutes.'

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:30.080
After the mix up at the airstrip, Saba wants to make sure their welcome to camp is flawless.

00:10:30.120 --> 00:10:32.040
Hi.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:37.600
I am so sorry, you guys, it was all the wrong airstrip.

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:38.680
Come and have a drink.

00:10:37.760 --> 00:10:39.120
Thank you.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.520
My name is Joe.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:41.880
Joe, I'm Saba.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:42.320
Hi.

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:42.760
Sonja.

00:10:41.880 --> 00:10:44.360
Hello, Sonja.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.520
Saba.

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.280
Welcome.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.800
So, this is part of the team.

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:50.520
This is the people who do rooms and kitchen and spotter guys.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:59.920
The team must now do everything they can to make up for the shaky start.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:08.560
Everything has to be, you know, super, super, super, because basically, it doesn't matter if it's a, the flight... problem.

00:11:07.760 --> 00:11:11.880
It's our role, really, to make it work for them.

00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:20.360
Back in the field, the search for bullets continues.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:26.640
To catch the perpetrators, they need to find as many undamaged bullets as possible.

00:11:27.200 --> 00:11:30.320
I've got another one in here, definitely.

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:31.720
You've got one there as well?

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.640
Here's another here.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:37.640
CONTINUOUS BEEPING Wow, it's everywhere.

00:11:38.200 --> 00:11:41.160
This is the one that can give us the best clues.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:55.200
You can actually see the scratch marks made by the rifling and this will be an absolute indicator of which rifle it came from.

00:11:54.400 --> 00:12:08.320
If the police can find the rifle, they can also compare this in their ballistic department and see if there's a match, so it's a very useful piece of hard evidence if it ever comes to a court trial.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:12.440
Iain will send these bullets to the police.

00:12:11.480 --> 00:12:14.240
They've found the evidence.

00:12:13.440 --> 00:12:17.760
Now they need to catch the poachers.

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:27.800
At camp, guests Joe and Sonja, have settled in.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:32.640
Alfred's about to take them on their first safari.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:36.840
Alf.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:38.880
Yes.

00:12:38.280 --> 00:12:39.880
Hi.

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:45.360
I want to make sure they have a really nice time, because of that whole airport mess up...

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:45.920
I know.

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:47.480
..Because they've been so sweet about it...

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:49.120
I know.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:53.640
..And I thought maybe if we can do a really lovely game drive and I'll try and do something special for them in the evening...

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:55.400
In the evening.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:55.920
We'll do something.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:56.360
We'll see.

00:12:55.400 --> 00:12:57.320
Yeah?

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:03.520
But Joe and Sonja are here to see elephants, and that's easier said than done.

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.160
All right, to go.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:16.160
In the drought, elephants break into smaller groups to make the most of the poor grazing.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:22.120
They can travel up to 50 miles a day in search of food.

00:13:21.240 --> 00:13:26.360
Alfred's got a tough job on his hands.

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:34.120
With one set of guests taken care of, Saba now has more on the way.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:36.600
They're here to see elephants too.

00:13:36.520 --> 00:13:40.240
They're arriving in about four minutes.

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:47.160
Saba is feeling the pressure.

00:13:47.800 --> 00:13:54.040
So, I'm just getting some nice drinks ready for them, so that when they arrive, they've got fresh juice.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:59.240
Wildlife guide, Bernard, is entertaining his guests on the way back from the airstrip.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.880
OK, this is how we are going to do it.

00:14:00.120 --> 00:14:05.680
We're going to allocate points for every animal that we spot.

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.200
Depending on how elusive they are, they get more points.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.400
OK.

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:12.480
Bernard is looking after them whilst they're here and he's with them the whole time.

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:22.920
So from, you know, six in the morning until about six in the evening when they come back, so they're getting real specialist care this week.

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:29.400
Elephants or not, Bernard is making sure his guests have a great time.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.280
They're very happy.

00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:32.400
Really, really happy.

00:14:31.560 --> 00:14:36.040
It's been a long day, but they've really enjoyed it.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:39.160
I-I've done my part.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.720
Come in, everyone.

00:14:41.920 --> 00:14:44.600
Have you all had some juice?

00:14:43.640 --> 00:14:44.880
Yes.

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:56.680
For Saba, making a success of the business is important, not just to balance the books but to help the elephants.

00:14:55.920 --> 00:15:04.200
The more guests that visit, the more people understand and love these endangered creatures.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:15.600
Over 900 elephants pass through the reserve, but in the drought they spread far and wide in search of food.

00:15:14.960 --> 00:15:23.160
The further they travel from the protected area, the closer they come to roads and towns.

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:25.240
This is where ivory poachers are most active.

00:15:24.320 --> 00:15:30.640
Frank is trying to catch them.

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:38.240
He's joined Chris Leadismo, head of the anti-poaching unit.

00:15:37.760 --> 00:15:41.800
Turn to the right, all out.

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:46.440
Just a couple of years ago, this place was a total killing ground.

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:52.720
These hills here, we lost around 30 elephants in just a couple of months there.

00:15:51.920 --> 00:16:01.400
These are not Kenya Wildlife service guys, these are not private guns and boots, these are community guys that have been pulled together, they've been given a structure with which to work.

00:16:00.520 --> 00:16:07.960
It's a completely grassroots, ground up initiative and that's what makes it so powerful.

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:12.600
And the importance of that can't be overstated because look at how enormous this landscape is.

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:20.440
Without the people that live here being the forces that protect it, you've got no hope.

00:16:20.400 --> 00:16:28.680
These community rangers know every inch of this terrain.

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:31.720
If anyone can track down poachers, they can.

00:16:30.920 --> 00:16:38.680
Inside the reserve, Alfred and his guests are looking for elephants.

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:41.440
They've been searching for two hours.

00:16:41.920 --> 00:16:45.560
That's a dik-dik.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:50.480
SHE GASPS So there's two of them there.

00:16:50.160 --> 00:16:51.520
Quite gregarious.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.760
Are they?

00:16:57.720 --> 00:16:58.880
OK.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:04.200
They're cute, but not what the guests came to see.

00:17:03.520 --> 00:17:15.079
Elephant Watch Camp with no elephants is bad for business.

00:17:19.119 --> 00:17:20.640
Bernard heads out to join the search.

00:17:19.839 --> 00:17:33.760
So that's our responsibility - to make sure that they enjoy their safari to the fullest because, you know, you feel like...

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:46.000
I want them to have the best experience, I want them to enjoy their safari, because people come here maybe once in a lifetime, and if you give them the best safari then it's good for them.

00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:49.240
I mean, you feel like you've given them something so special.

00:17:50.120 --> 00:18:00.680
Saba hopes that their time here will inspire her guests to help elephants.

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:11.760
We want to give them a very meaningful experience with elephants and there's, you know, there's so much happening with the elephants right now, it can't really fail to be meaningful.

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:21.520
And seeing what's happening to them, not only with the poaching but with the drought, which is making life a lot harder than it is normally.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:36.080
Elephants are resilient animals, they can survive all but the worst of droughts, but they're powerless against guns.

00:18:36.200 --> 00:18:42.760
With a single pair of tusks worth up to $100,000, elephants are in big trouble.

00:18:42.880 --> 00:18:53.840
Frank and the anti-poaching team want to make sure that no more elephants are harmed.

00:18:53.000 --> 00:18:58.520
They're patrolling an area where poachers often enter the reserve.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:02.240
How often will you walk here?

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:02.800
Very often.

00:19:01.960 --> 00:19:04.280
Four days a week?

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:13.680
Just down this river?

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:23.760
These community rangers use their local knowledge and traditional tracking skills to catch ivory poachers.

00:19:23.000 --> 00:19:33.240
Just the fact that these guys are out walking, the poachers are also watching everyone's tracks and here they can see, "Hey, this is a...

00:19:32.400 --> 00:19:33.600
"This is a heavy patrol that's come through here, you know.

00:19:32.640 --> 00:19:35.560
"We're in danger.

00:19:34.840 --> 00:19:36.920
We're going to stay away from this area."

00:19:36.120 --> 00:19:39.480
So there's a, kind of, a dual role.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:49.880
Having left tracks in the dry riverbed, they climb a nearby hill for a better vantage point.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:55.200
From up here they can see poachers coming for miles.

00:19:56.760 --> 00:20:04.880
This is where these guys keep a lookout for any movement and then anything they see they'll report to the headquarters.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:18.520
As much as we're trying to win this battle for elephants through hearts and minds, at the end of the day, you need law enforcement and that's what these guys are doing.

00:20:17.800 --> 00:20:26.320
Community patrols are a key part of the plan to stop ivory poaching.

00:20:25.480 --> 00:20:33.920
If they get it right in Samburu, then this model can be used to help protect elephants elsewhere in Africa.

00:20:33.200 --> 00:20:36.560
Tourism is also crucial.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:48.960
A thriving safari industry will ensure that elephants are more valuable alive than dead.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:52.120
Alfred has finally found what he's looking for.

00:20:52.800 --> 00:20:54.480
My zoom is too big, that says it all.

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:59.200
I have to change the lens to take a picture.

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:07.000
The most amazing thing here is really the closeness and the quietness with which you're here and you can face them.

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:07.800
It's very, very unique.

00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:09.720
It's precious.

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:19.880
Wow.

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:20.680
S That is so...

00:21:29.720 --> 00:21:30.840
He's sitting on the other one.

00:21:29.960 --> 00:21:31.440
Look at them.

00:21:30.480 --> 00:21:35.160
This is the best sight I've ever seen of elephants, it's gorgeous.

00:21:34.480 --> 00:21:36.600
S Look at them.

00:21:48.320 --> 00:22:06.160
Samburu is one of the few places in the world where people can be this close to elephants... ..but their trusting nature can also leave them vulnerable when they move beyond the reserve.

00:22:05.440 --> 00:22:11.240
Frank gets a call from the community rangers.

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:19.160
Three, perhaps four alleged poachers were spotted and they ran from their camp.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:29.000
They fit the profiles, four young guys, they've got a sack with lots of stuff in it, so we're just going to go and see if we can help the search from the air.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:43.000
Frank has been joined by a sergeant from the Kenya Wildlife Service.

00:22:50.080 --> 00:22:56.960
The rest of the anti-poaching team are searching on the ground.

00:22:56.040 --> 00:22:59.200
Fighting poachers is dangerous.

00:22:58.240 --> 00:23:04.680
In the last 12 months, over 20 rangers have been killed in Africa.

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:07.200
Saba is worried.

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:14.240
In some cases, aeroplanes have been shot at in the past, but...you know, one has to be careful.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:16.000
So just...

00:23:15.040 --> 00:23:17.920
Just plenty of circles.

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:28.360
'I worry about Frank, I worry about Chris Leadismo, who's our ranger.'

00:23:27.400 --> 00:23:45.800
I worry about all of them because you know they're out there, they're right on the frontline, and there have been many occasions where they have had very close contact with the poachers, they have been in the sights of their guns.

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:53.520
The poachers have been scared off, but the rangers will remain on full alert.

00:23:57.840 --> 00:24:04.360
The search also yields some unexpected results.

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:12.640
I'm seeing a herd of 40 elephants!

00:24:12.080 --> 00:24:17.080
They're not far from camp, but they're on the other side of the river.

00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:24.040
This is valuable information for Saba and her team.

00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:26.040
Now, all they have to do is find a way across.

00:24:34.320 --> 00:24:35.600
Bernard is heading out to look for a good spot.

00:24:34.800 --> 00:24:41.760
Saba has sent me out to find a place that we can cross to the other side of the river.

00:24:40.920 --> 00:24:49.160
I know it's a bit difficult for Land Cruisers because they're heavy cars, but we're going to give it a try anyway.

00:24:50.920 --> 00:24:59.880
The elephants are tantalisingly close, but this river is notorious for its sinking sand.

00:25:08.360 --> 00:25:10.240
Uh-oh.

00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:10.520
Getting stuck.

00:25:22.160 --> 00:25:23.760
I'm just going to...check it out.

00:25:25.080 --> 00:25:26.120
This has no grip, you know.

00:25:25.560 --> 00:25:32.080
You try to roll, but nothing happens because the car has no strong grip.

00:25:38.160 --> 00:25:40.440
Saba, Saba, do you read?

00:25:39.480 --> 00:25:40.680
Oh, no.

00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:41.680
What's happened?

00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:42.040
'Echo Whisky Camp, this is Bernard, do you read?'

00:25:41.320 --> 00:25:43.480
Hi B, go ahead.

00:25:42.760 --> 00:25:45.960
Hi, Sabs.

00:25:45.200 --> 00:25:46.320
Erm...

00:25:45.400 --> 00:25:50.160
A little bit of bad news - I'm stuck in the river.

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:53.120
We were trying to cross at that spot I was telling you about and I'm stuck.

00:25:52.200 --> 00:25:53.680
Erm...

00:25:53.040 --> 00:25:57.320
How stuck?

00:25:56.440 --> 00:25:57.960
'Very, very stuck.'

00:25:57.640 --> 00:25:59.960
Oh, Lordy.

00:25:59.080 --> 00:26:02.880
Then I'll be with you in five minutes.

00:26:02.000 --> 00:26:07.960
Oh, no, he's got stuck.

00:26:11.120 --> 00:26:12.360
Darling, I have to go and rescue Bernard.

00:26:19.480 --> 00:26:21.680
Oh, God, I can see you!

00:26:35.120 --> 00:26:36.240
Woo!

00:26:36.000 --> 00:26:37.080
Woo!

00:26:36.400 --> 00:26:41.640
They're out, but that doesn't solve the problem.

00:26:41.000 --> 00:26:43.120
Let me just get out and have a look.

00:26:42.320 --> 00:26:46.720
So we need to find somewhere else.

00:26:46.040 --> 00:26:47.160
Yes, this is not good enough.

00:26:46.360 --> 00:26:57.640
Unless they can find a crossing point, elephant watching is off the agenda.

00:26:58.640 --> 00:27:11.440
Though coming at it from different angles, both Saba and Frank want to see a large, healthy and safe population of elephants in Samburu.

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:17.400
Frank's team is starting to make some progress.

00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:20.440
Poaching is way down in this area.

00:27:19.480 --> 00:27:27.440
But from here, what we've gotta do is consolidate the gains we've made and make sure that we don't slip back.

00:27:27.120 --> 00:27:33.880
The problem is ever escalating because the price of ivory, there's no sign of the price of ivory decreasing yet.

00:27:32.920 --> 00:27:37.320
And as long as that price keeps rising, we can't stop work.

00:27:36.560 --> 00:27:44.240
We've gotta keep going and we've gotta keep making what we do more and more effective.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:48.560
But all their hard work is beginning to pay off.

00:27:47.600 --> 00:27:48.840
There's been a breakthrough.

00:27:48.240 --> 00:27:54.600
Three poachers have been caught and are being held in the local jail.

00:27:53.800 --> 00:28:02.080
The ballistics evidence that Iain, Frank and the team provided could help put them behind bars.

00:28:01.760 --> 00:28:09.400
Next time, there's an emergency as sandstorms hit camp.

00:28:08.480 --> 00:28:14.520
It's really hard to have dinner when you feel like you're in a Saharan dust storm.

00:28:13.560 --> 00:28:20.120
An orphan elephant and her baby need Frank's help.

00:28:19.360 --> 00:28:22.800
She's just taken off in a straight line towards an area which is pretty dangerous for her.

00:28:21.880 --> 00:28:25.880
And Saba takes charge of the river crossings.

00:28:25.000 --> 00:28:27.920
Are you ready, team?

00:28:31.000 --> 00:28:32.800
Yeah.

00:28:31.920 --> 00:28:35.400
We could be playing golf somewhere!
